<title>USA: Illinois 1996 jobless rate at 5.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Illinois 1996 jobless rate at 5.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>- Illinois' unemployment rate averaged 5.2 percent during 11 months of 1996, tying the rate reported for 1995, according to the state's department of employment security.</p>
<p>The department reported the state gained 93,000 manufacturing, transportation and service industry jobs, an increase of 1.8 percent over 1995. In 1995, Illinois added 100,600 jobs, a 2.5 percent increase over 1994.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
</text>
